# YouTube Subtitle Maker

> ⚡️ Download YouTube audio, transcribe locally with OpenAI Whisper, and (optionally) translate subtitles with Google Gemini or any OpenAI-compatible API — all in a sleek desktop app.

**Version**: 2.0.0-alpha  
**License**: *(pending)*

---

## What is this?

A cross-platform desktop application built as a **pnpm monorepo** that combines:

- **Python FastAPI backend** — Handles YouTube audio extraction, local speech-to-text with OpenAI Whisper, subtitle translation, and SRT file generation.
- **Expo + Tamagui + Tauri frontend** — A modern, responsive desktop UI rendered in a native Tauri 2 shell.

The app runs entirely on your machine: audio processing and transcription happen **locally** (no cloud STT costs), while translation optionally taps into remote AI APIs.

---

## Features

- **YouTube Audio Download** — Extract audio via yt-dlp (supports age-gated/private videos with browser cookies).
- **Local Transcription** — OpenAI Whisper runs on-device (GPU/CPU). Choose from multiple model sizes.
- **YouTube Captions Fallback** — Skip Whisper entirely and reuse YouTube's own captions when available.
- **AI Translation** — Translate subtitles via Google Gemini, OpenAI, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (e.g., LM Studio).
- **Multi-SRT Library** — Re-transcribe or re-translate the same video multiple times without re-downloading audio.
- **MPV Integration** — Play generated videos with subtitles directly from the app.
- **Streamed Progress** — Real-time progress updates during download, transcription, and translation.
- **Modern Desktop UI** — Glass-morphism design, keyboard navigation, responsive layout, and first-run dependency checker.

---

## Tech Stack

### Backend (`backend/`)
| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python 3.11–3.13 | Runtime |
| FastAPI | HTTP API framework |
| Uvicorn | ASGI server |
| OpenAI Whisper | Local speech-to-text |
| yt-dlp | YouTube audio extraction |
| Google GenAI / OpenAI | Translation providers |
| PyTorch | Whisper inference backend |
| pytest | Testing |
| ruff | Linting & formatting |
| PyInstaller | Backend bundling for desktop |

### Frontend (`apps/desktop/`)
| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| React 18.2 | UI framework |
| React Native Web | Cross-platform rendering |
| Expo SDK 51 | Tooling & routing |
| Tamagui 1.115 | UI components & design tokens |
| Tauri 2 | Desktop shell (Rust) |
| Zustand | State management |

### Shared Packages
- `packages/api-client` — Typed TypeScript client mirroring the backend API.
- `packages/ui` — Tamagui design system components shared across the frontend.

---

## Prerequisites

- **Python** 3.11, 3.12, or 3.13 *(3.14 is NOT supported — PyTorch lacks wheels)*
- **Node.js** ≥ 20
- **pnpm** ≥ 10
- **Rust** (with `rustup`) — required for Tauri
- **ffmpeg** — required by Whisper
- **mpv** — for the "play with subtitles" feature
- **deno** or **node** — yt-dlp needs a JS runtime for YouTube deobfuscation

> **Note**: `cargo`/`rustc`/`tauri` may not be on PATH in non-interactive shells. Run `source "$HOME/.cargo/env"` first.

---

## Installation

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Kidemi04/yt-subtitle-maker.git
cd yt-subtitle-maker
```

### 2. Set up the backend

```bash
# Creates backend/.venv and installs all Python dependencies
# (downloads ~2 GB of PyTorch — may take a while)
PYTHON=python3.12 scripts/setup-backend.sh
```

### 3. Install frontend dependencies

```bash
pnpm install
```

---

## Development

### Quick Start (recommended)

```bash
pnpm dev
```

Opens two macOS Terminal windows:
- **"yt backend"** — uvicorn with auto-reload on `127.0.0.1:8000`
- **"yt web"** — Expo web dev server on `http://localhost:8081`

Then open `http://localhost:8081` in your browser.

> **macOS Automation permission**: On first run, macOS may ask to allow "Terminal wants to control Terminal" — click **Allow**.

### Dev with native Tauri window

```bash
pnpm -F desktop tauri:dev
```

Spawns the backend, the web UI, and wraps them in a native desktop window. All logs in one terminal.

### Web UI only (no backend)

```bash
pnpm web
# → http://localhost:8081
```

### Backend only (manual)

```bash
cd backend
../backend/.venv/bin/python -m uvicorn api.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --reload
```

---

## Building

### Packaged desktop app

```bash
pnpm -F desktop tauri:build
```

Outputs:
- **macOS**: `apps/desktop/src-tauri/target/release/bundle/macos/`
- **DMG**: `apps/desktop/src-tauri/target/release/bundle/dmg/`

### Rebuild just the backend bundle

```bash
pnpm -F desktop build:backend
```

Generates `apps/desktop/src-tauri/backend-dist/` (used by Tauri bundling).

---

## Testing

### Backend tests

```bash
# Run all tests
backend/.venv/bin/python -m pytest

# Run a specific test
backend/.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/api/test_process.py::test_name -v
```

### Backend lint

```bash
backend/.venv/bin/ruff check backend
```

### Frontend typecheck

```bash
pnpm -F desktop typecheck
```

