## Architecture

### Backend — thin routes over a modular core

`backend/api/main.py` wires together routers (`metadata`, `process`, `translator`, `version`, `config`, `dependencies`, `library`, `history`, `cookies`, `engines`, `system`, `fs`). All business logic lives in `backend/core/`:

| Module | Role |
|---|---|
| `core/pipeline.py` | Main orchestrator: fetch metadata → select STT → download → transcribe → [translate] → write SRT |
| `core/downloader/` | yt-dlp wrapper, browser cookie support, JS runtime probing |
| `core/stt/` | Pluggable transcription engines (Whisper, YouTube captions) |
| `core/translator/` | Pluggable translation (Gemini, OpenAI, local OpenAI) |
| `core/library_runs.py` | Multi-SRT library management with concurrent-safe file ops |
| `core/dependency_manager.py` | Whisper model downloader, ffmpeg/mpv checker |
| `core/config.py` | Pydantic-settings config persisted to `~/.yt_subtitle_tool/config.json` |

### Frontend — Expo Router + Tamagui

| Route | Screen |
|---|---|
| `index.tsx` | Generate (main workflow) |
| `library.tsx` | Library & video history |
| `history.tsx` | Global run history |
| `settings.tsx` | App settings |
| `init.tsx` | First-run dependency checker |
| `about.tsx` | About page |
| `_layout.tsx` | Shell (sidebar, topbar, logs drawer) |

State lives in Zustand stores under `apps/desktop/src/state/`.

### Tauri Shell

`apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs` manages the backend subprocess:
- **Debug** — spawns local Python virtualenv's uvicorn
- **Release** — launches the PyInstaller-bundled binary
- Both modes check `127.0.0.1:8000` first and attach if already running

---

## API Endpoints

The backend exposes the following route groups (all under `/api`):

- `GET /api/metadata` — Fetch YouTube video metadata
- `POST /api/process` — Run the full pipeline (streaming NDJSON events)
- `POST /api/translator/translate` — Translate SRT content
- `GET /api/version` — App version info
- `GET /api/config` / `POST /api/config` — App configuration
- `GET /api/dependencies` — Check/download runtime dependencies
- `GET /api/engines` — List available STT & translation engines
- `GET /api/library` / `POST /api/library/*` — Video library management
- `GET /api/history` — Processing history
- `POST /api/cookies` — Browser cookie import
- `POST /api/system/*` — System operations

---

## Project Structure

```
yt-subtitle-maker/
├── backend/                    # Python FastAPI backend
│   ├── api/                    # FastAPI routers & schemas
│   ├── core/                   # Business logic (pipeline, STT, translation, etc.)
│   ├── packaging/              # PyInstaller spec & entrypoint
│   └── pyproject.toml          # Python dependencies
├── apps/
│   └── desktop/                # Desktop frontend
│       ├── app/                # Expo Router pages
│       ├── src/
│       │   ├── components/     # UI components
│       │   ├── hooks/          # Custom React hooks
│       │   ├── lib/            # Utilities
│       │   └── state/          # Zustand stores
│       └── src-tauri/          # Tauri Rust shell
├── packages/
│   ├── api-client/             # Typed TS API client
│   └── ui/                     # Tamagui design system
├── scripts/                    # Dev & build scripts
├── tests/                      # Backend test suite
└── docs/superpowers/           # Design specs & implementation plans
```

---

## Configuration

App settings are persisted to:

```
~/.yt_subtitle_tool/config.json
```

Output folders (`output/`, `downloads/`) resolve relative to the backend's working directory:
- **Development**: `backend/`
- **Packaged app**: `~/.yt_subtitle_tool/`

